description.en:
Returns the match's progress milestone. The engine raises it as the match goes on and never lowers it:
- 100 once the first half is under way;
- 200 on a second signal of the first period (not identified);
- 300 once a later period (1 to 4) has started;
- 400 or 500 for period 5.
So a value of 100 means the match is still in its first half. CMND_BTL_SET_MATCH_PHASE raises it, and CMND_BTL_SET_MATCHPHASE can write it directly.

examples.code:
// Called by the engine at each kick-off after a goal. The event runs once,
// when the player's team (0) has one goal and the match is still in its
// first half.
CallMatchKickoffRestart <- function ()
{
	if (CMND_BTL_GET_POINT(0) == 1 && CMND_BTL_GET_MATCHPHASE() == 100 && eventCounter == 0)
	{
		ev44130070_Run();
		eventCounter++;
	}
};
